## Folder system

```
Templates/            ← master resume + cover letter source. Never sent directly.
Applications/
  application_index.csv          ← master tracking sheet, one row per application
                                     columns: date,company,position,location,status,
                                     resume_path,cover_letter_path,notes_path,posting_link
  outreach_log.csv                ← real outreach actually sent (not drafts)
  blacklist.md                    ← optional do-not-apply list, checked by job-fit-eval
  YYYY-MM-DD_Company_Role/       ← one folder per application
    <YourName>_Resume_<Company>.pdf   ← what actually gets uploaded
    CoverLetter_<Company>.pdf          ← what actually gets uploaded
    *.tex                                ← editable source, kept next to the PDF
    job_posting.md                       ← the actual listing, saved verbatim
    notes.md                             ← what was tailored/changed and why, + status
scripts/                ← job-scan, set_status, pipeline_summary Python scripts
job_search_log.md      ← running log of postings already surfaced, avoids duplicate reports
```

## Skills available (Claude Code)

Installed at `~/.claude/skills/`, invocable directly or triggered automatically when the
situation matches:

| Skill | Use for |
|---|---|
| `job-fit-eval` | Score a posting against real verified skills, flag gaps honestly, recommend apply/skip. **Run this before tailoring anything.** |
| `tailor-application` | Draft a tailored resume + cover letter for a specific posting. |
| `company-research` | Structured research brief before a cover letter opener or an interview. |
| `linkedin-outreach` | Find a contact + draft a short outreach message (draft-only, never sends). |
| `follow-up-check` | Scan the tracker for applications overdue for a follow-up. |
| `job-scan` | Zero-token scan of `scripts/companies.json`'s curated company list via public ATS APIs. |
| `stop-slop` | Anti-AI-writing-pattern check, run on every cover letter and outreach draft. |

None of these auto-submit anything. Every one stops at "draft" and hands control back.

## Ethical rules

- **Never submit an application without you reviewing it first.** Draft, tailor, compile —
  you always click submit, never the assistant.
- **Discourage low-fit applications.** If `job-fit-eval` scores a posting below 3.0/5, say so
  plainly and explain why, rather than tailoring an application anyway.
- **Quality over quantity.** A handful of well-targeted applications beats a high-volume blast.

## Canonical application states

Source of truth: `scripts/states.py`. Use `scripts/set_status.py` to change a row's status —
never hand-edit `application_index.csv` for status changes.

| State | When to use |
|---|---|
| `Evaluated` | `job-fit-eval` has scored it, not yet drafted |
| `Drafted` | Resume/cover letter tailored, not yet sent |
| `Applied` | Sent — `set_status.py` asks for explicit confirmation before allowing this |
| `Responded` | Company replied |
| `Interview` | In interview process |
| `Offer` | Offer received |
| `Rejected` | Rejected by company |
| `Discarded` | You decided not to pursue further |
| `SKIP` | Evaluated but not worth applying |

